"Wi-Fi passphrase","Words containing parts of the name are excluded, as directory policies require.","Password Generator Help","About {0}","A sequence of random common words is both stronger and easier to type than a short jumble of symbols. The entropy readout shows how hard a password is to guess — each extra word multiplies the possibilities. On screen, a muted dot marks each space — the dot itself is never part of the password.","Entropy counts how many equally likely possibilities an attacker would have to try — every extra bit doubles them. Around 50 bits already means about a quadrillion possibilities: far beyond online guessing and impractical for most offline cracking. Each specification sets its own minimum so a comfortable-looking choice can never quietly be a weak one — word counts that cannot reach it are greyed out.",
